<title>FRANCE: Gle des Eaux to sell Blenheim stake.</title>
<headline>Gle des Eaux to sell Blenheim stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French utilities company Compagnie Generale des Eaux plans to sell its 15.4 percent stake in the current tender for shares in exhibition organiser Blenheim Plc, a spokesman for the French company said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Generale des Eaux plans to sell its shares in the tender,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The stake sale is part of the French group's programme of asset disposals, to help pay down its debt mountain which stood at 56.3 billion francs at the end of the first half 1996.</p>
<p>British newspaper group United News &amp; Media Plc said on Tuesday it has made an agreed offer for Blenheim at five stg per share, valuing the company at 592.5 million stg. United said it already has acceptances for 51 percent of the shares.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
